# WHAT GROWS, AS TEXT. A tree is not drawn here: these are the numbers its growth is worked out from.
#
#   tree NAME biomes B... form F height MIN MAX slender S limbs N levels L spread DEG rise R droop D leaf CELLS flat K bark M colour M share W
#
# form: spreading  the trunk gives out into limbs, limbs into branches (an oak)
#       conifer    the trunk goes all the way up, whorls of short branches around it (a pine)
#       palm       a bare leaning stem, fronds at the top
#       column     a stem with arms and no leaves (a cactus)
#       bush       no trunk to speak of
#       snag       dead: branches and nothing on them
#
# The formulas (WorldMap.cpp, grow_tree):
#   how thick:   d = (H / S)^(3/2)                 a column of wood buckles under itself past H = c d^(2/3) (Greenhill, McMahon).
#                                                  `slender` is how close to that this kind lives: larger is thinner.
#   the taper:   r(z) = r0 (1 - z/H)^(3/4)         and a flare at the roots, that dies away as e^(-z)
#   a fork:      r_child = r / sqrt(n)             the pipe model: the wood going up is the wood going on (da Vinci)
#                l_child = l (r_child / r)^(2/3)   elastic similarity: a longer branch must be thicker
#   a branch:    turned by `rise` toward the light each step, and bent down by its own weight as a cantilever does, in
#                proportion to (l / r)^2 up to where it has stiffened, times `droop`.
#   the next one round: 137.5 degrees on from the last (phyllotaxis).
#
#   land BIOME big B small S flora F        how thickly big trees (a stand every 10 m), small ones, and plants grow there
#   flora NAME biomes B... height H colour M share W     what grows on the ground: one to a cell
#
# colour and bark are `material` (Terrain.hpp). Barks 16 birch, 17 dark, 18 red, 19 palm; leaves
# 20 deep, 21 bright, 22 yellow-green, 23 orange, 24 red, 25 pink, 26 blue-green, 27 silver; 28 yellow, 29 white, 30 purple, 31 scarlet.

land Forest    big 0.62 small 0.16 flora 0.07
land Jungle    big 0.85 small 0.35 flora 0.14
land Taiga     big 0.5  small 0.12 flora 0.03
land Swamp     big 0.45 small 0.3  flora 0.10
land Grassland big 0.10 small 0.12 flora 0.10
land Savanna   big 0.14 small 0.10 flora 0.04
land Desert    big 0.05 small 0.06 flora 0.012
land Tundra    big 0.0  small 0.10 flora 0.03
land Mountain  big 0.10 small 0.08 flora 0.01
land Beach     big 0.12 small 0.02 flora 0.01

